      "text": "First, since $AB$ is a diameter of the circle, an angle inscribed in a semicircle is always a right angle. So, $$\\angle BAC = 90^\\circ.$$ Next, let $M$ be the midpoint of $AB$. Since $OM \\perp AB$, our triangle $OMA$ is a right triangle. It follows that $$\\angle OMA = 90^\\circ - \\angle {AMO},$$ and since $$\\angle AMO = \\frac{\\angle{B}{AM}}{2}=\\frac{\\angle BAE}{2} \\tag*{$\\square$},$$ we can conclude that $$\\angle OMA = 90^\\circ -\\frac{\\angle BAE}{2}=90^\\circ - \\frac{43^\\circ}{2}=43.5^\\circ.$$ It follows that $$\\angle DMC =\\angle{OMA} = 43.5^\\circ.$$ Since $CD \\parallel{OA}$, they have the same measure, so $\\angle CED = 2 \\cdot \\angle DMC = \\boxed{87^\\circ}$. The answer is 87",
